<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39248" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδῐκ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>adjudge property in dispute to</i> one, of the judge,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. κλῆρόν</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Is.
				11.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				48.26
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδεδικασμένου καὶ ἔχοντος
				τὸν</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῆρον</span>
			<i>having had</i> it <i>adjudged to one</i> and being in
			possession, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				43.7
			</span></i>: abs., Lexib.<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. 
				Med.
			, of the claimant, <i>go to law to establish</i>
			<i>one's claim</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				874a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGnom.</u>
				28
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				40
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω . . τὸν κλῆρον</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδικασάμενος</span> I have obtained it
				<i>by a lawsuit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				11.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. c.gen.,
				<i>sue for, claim at law</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδικάζεσθαι τοῦ κλήρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				3.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				43.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῆς ἐπικλήρου</span>
			<i>claim the hand of</i> the heiress, ib.<i><span class="en">
				55
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				10.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιδικαζόμενος, ὁ</span>, title of plays by <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῆς ἀρχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					19.2.1
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῆς μέσης χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1107b31
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be assigned</i>, of an heiress, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				12.18
			</span></i>.</div>
